  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lifesaving, Empowerment and Resilience Project (LEARP) for Conflict-Affected Communities in Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project primarily aims to address the urgent and life-saving needs of women and girls but also men and boys (where there is disclosure) who have experienced incidents of sexual violence, including conflict-related sexual violence (CRSV), in conflict-affected areas of Northeast and Northwest Nigeria. The focus will be on providing comprehensive, survivor-centered services - through a coordinated Gender Based Violence (GBV) case management process linking survivors to medical care (including sexual and reproductive health and clinical management of rape), mental health and psychosocial support, tailored assistance (cash support, dignity kits) and referrals. Concurrently, the project will empower at-risk individuals through vocational skills training and economic empowerment, strengthen government authorities, women-led groups, community-based protection structures, and foster long-term resilience and sustainability through coordinated, integrated actions among partners.</narrative>
  </description>
